      "note": "The phases tell the reader where a run is, but not whether it is stuck. The writing counter runs on a fixed timer and never waits for Lynx (sa-push-changes.service.ts:145-150, :206-211), so it cannot stall. The read-back is where a slow or silent Lynx shows, and it looks the same either way. The status line stays on \"Retrieving latest Percent Adjustments from Lynx for comparison\" while each of three Lynx requests waits up to three 60-second attempts with 5-second gaps (cloud-service-base.ts:43-45, :372-463), roughly nine and a half minutes at worst. If they all fail, the progress dialog closes with no result line (sa-main-toolbar.component.ts:174-178), and the only message is a \"Lynx Cloud Error\" (or \"Lynx Drive Error\") toast reading \"Incomplete or invalid data was received from Lynx.\" (sa-dashboard.component.ts:305-314).",
