      "note": "Transform 12 moved this sentence onto the write phase, and on production it is wrong there. Each write is fire-and-forget. processItem sends the change and returns immediately (sa-push-changes.service.ts:206-211), and neither the Lynx Cloud nor the Lynx Drive implementation waits for an answer (lynx-cloud.service.ts:80-95, lynx-drive.service.ts:67-87). The counter advances on the fixed per-station delay (:145-150) whatever the connection is doing, so a stall cannot show here. Writing costs at least 100 ms a station, about 15 s on a 148-station course. \"Slowest phase\" is not established either: the next phase waits for three sequential Lynx responses, each allowed three 60-second attempts (cloud-service-base.ts:43-45, :372-463). A dead connection shows in that phase.",
